nT. Nonnenmacher\n\nT. Nonnenmacher\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nImage\n\nDownload full-text PDFRead full-text\n\n## Abstract\n\nConsidering the Grad moment ansatz as a suitable ﬁrst approximation to a closed ﬁnite-moment dynamics, the correction is derived from the Boltzmann equation. The correction consists of two parts, local and nonlocal. Locally corrected thirteen-moment equations are demonstrated to contain exact transport coefﬁcients. Equations resulting from the nonlocal correction give a microscopic justiﬁcation to some phenomenological theories of extended hydrodynamics.\n\n\nDynamic correction to moment approximations\n\nIliya V. Karlin*and Alexander N. Gorban\n\nComputing Center RAS, Krasnoyarsk, 660036, Russian Federation\n\nG. Dukek and T. F. Nonnenmacher\n\nDepartment of Mathematical Physics, University of Ulm, D-89069 Ulm, Germany\n\n~Received 13 January 1997!\n\nConsidering the Grad moment ansatz as a suitable ﬁrst approximation to a closed ﬁnite-moment dynamics,\n\nthe correction is derived from the Boltzmann equation. The correction consists of two parts, local and nonlocal.\n\nLocally corrected thirteen-moment equations are demonstrated to contain exact transport coefﬁcients. Equa-\n\ntions resulting from the nonlocal correction give a microscopic justiﬁcation to some phenomenological theories\n\nof extended hydrodynamics. @S1063-651X~98!03502-8#\n\nPACS number~s!: 05.60.1 w, 44.10.1 i, 47.10.1 g, 51.10.1 y\n\nA considerable part of the modern development of non-\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegular and chaotic motion in softened gravitational systems | Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society | Oxford Academic (https://academic.oup.com/mnras/article/331/1/23/1034232)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 24.6 years ago; Crawled: last week; ### 1.1 Softening and the collisionless Boltzmann equation ... Braun & Hepp 1977;